## Owner directive

**FIRST IMPLEMENTATION, THEN CORRECTION.** Implement the complete required
production driver, 100%, before starting the zero-failure lint milestone.
This is the highest-priority umbrella TODO and takes precedence over
lint-only cleanup, speculative hardening and conflicting older hold language.

The owner wants the first notebook run to exercise the entire implementation,
including cross-component complexity. Do not make a partial subsystem perfect
while leaving required paths absent. Failed launch, crash or runtime failure
in an owner-authorized test is evidence for the next fix, not a prerequisite
that must be eliminated through indefinite source-only polishing. Implement
the full intended behavior, then validate to zero failures, pass CI and iterate
on actual notebook logs. Never equate this tolerance of test failures with
permission to fabricate readiness or leave known implementations missing.

The integration agent prioritizes runtime implementation and wiring; other
coordinating agents resolve Clang-Tidy and validator findings without weakening
checks or imposing a serial lint-only hold on the missing source work.

