## Initial EDMA activation connection — 2026-11-10

The native `SimpleATH` queue adoption now attempts the **real**
`NativeQueues::startGated()` only if its same-epoch physical RF/channel,
station-MAC and live RF-kill callback permits reception. If radio proof is
not present, the coherent queues stay mapped in `Prepared` with DMA and IRQ
masked; a later power-on can retry without treating mapping as receiver
readiness. The initial-start gate explicitly excludes the `Prepared` state
borrowed by the WPA2 key-update isolation/restart flow. The queue executor
rechecks the live RF gate before enabling PCI bus mastering and again before
unmasking interrupts, quarantining/recovering a partial start on revocation.

This closes only the missing **initial EDMA start invocation**; the physical
receive-only RF pipeline is **still not connected** to the native owner. It
must first obtain an independently verified board crystal, exact channel
regulatory approval, and Bluetooth antenna/coexistence lease before asserting
radio/channel readiness. No receive scan, TX, AirDrop, hardware test, kext
build/tag, or USB/EFI installation follows from this source change. Strict
native source syntax passed on the pinned research SDK; the whole-tree
zero-failure validator remains outstanding.

A subsequent native interrupt-path correction also fails the *running* EDMA
lease closed when the live RF-kill/physical radio callback is revoked: check
before servicing the interrupt and after completing any RX/TX callback, before
rearming the device IER. A failed gate enters the existing DMA fault/physical
isolation path rather than merely dropping received frames while MAC/automatic
responses might continue. This is source-only interrupt-time enforcement; it
does not replace a hardware RF-kill IRQ or prove on-device switching behavior.
